    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0671" n="638" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v24/pg638"/>

                <head>219. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Jordan<anchor n="1" xml:id="d219-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1970-09-10T15:10:00+00:00">September 10, 1970,
                        1510Z</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>147976. Ref.: State 147736; Amman 4521.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d219-f2"/> Subject:
                    Hijacking.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>You should proceed to suggest to King Hussein that he pass warning to
                            PFLP of direst of consequences if any
                        of hostages should be harmed.</item>
                    <pb facs="0672" n="639" xml:id="pg639"/>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Unanimous decision of UNSC September 9 and expressions of outrage not only
                        in West but also in East Bloc can be cited as indication of harm done
                        overall Arab image by current detention hundreds of innocent travellers. Any
                        harm to these could only heighten this feeling to detriment of overall Arab
                        position.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#bold">Rogers</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d219-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d219-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Files
                    1970–73, AV 12. Secret; Immediate; Nodis.
                    Drafted by Davies; cleared by U. Alexis Johnson and Curran (S/S); and
                    approved by Sisco.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d219-f2" n="2" xml:id="d219-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 147736 to Amman, September 10, 0032Z. (Ibid.) Telegram 4521 is <ref
                        target="#d217">Document 217</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
